-- Run this ONLY after the submit-lead Edge Function is deployed and the
-- frontend has been switched to call it (RequestMachineForm.jsx uses
-- supabase.functions.invoke('submit-lead', ...) instead of a direct
-- supabase.from('leads').insert(...)). Until then, this will break the
-- live request form.
--
-- Today the anon key can insert directly into `leads` from any browser
-- or script, with no rate limiting. Once the Edge Function (which uses
-- the service_role key, bypassing RLS) is the only inserter, anon no
-- longer needs - and should not have - direct insert access.
--
-- "Allow anon insert" below is a placeholder - this repo can't see your
-- actual policy name. Check Supabase Dashboard -> Authentication ->
-- Policies -> leads for the real name of the anon insert policy and
-- substitute it before running this.
drop policy if exists "Allow anon insert" on public.leads;

-- Leaves `leads` with RLS enabled and no policies for anon/authenticated,
-- so only service_role (the Edge Function) can read or write it.
